## Context budget

Conversation history usually dominates the window. Prefer a **new chat** when the phase changes (`/sc-discuss` → `/sc-run` → `/sc-ship`). Do not continue a long discuss thread into AFK run. Hand off with the one-line next action only (state, blockers, dirty git, next pickup).

## Lane Detection

| User intent | Lane / action |
|-------------|---------------|
| Ask, clarify, visual draft, consult, research, decide | Advisory → Agent + `/sc-discuss` when mission-scoped |
| Add, build, create, implement, feature | Mission → Agent + `/sc-run` after discuss clear |
| Fix, debug, diagnose, broken, error, bug, crash | Debug → Cursor Debug Mode |
| Edit prompt/config/doc, small fix, just commit; one-off polish/optimize/refactor/adjust | Quick → Agent + `/sc-quick` |
| Batched polish (≥3 backlog items or explicit batch discuss) | Mission → Agent + `/sc-run` after discuss clear |
| Ship | Agent + `/sc-ship` |

No non-blocking questions mid-AFK. Detail skills: `sc-discuss`, `sc-run`, `sc-ship`, `sc-quick`, `sc-mission`.

## Lifecycle

```
/sc-discuss (HIL clear) → new session /sc-run → human check → /sc-ship
```

- **Discuss** → `clarify-status clear`. Handoff: `Spec clear. New session: /sc-run.`
- **Run** → plan → design-contract → approved-scenarios → build → combine (static + diff-cov + mutation) → fix → browser-probe (UI/workflow) → review + `sc-judge` → `ready`. Handoff: `Ready. Human check, then /sc-ship.` Optional post-ready drain via `sc-post-ready-drain` (git-primary; no GitHub PR needed) after ready and before `/sc-ship`. Optional post-ready fat-diff hygiene via `sc-split-to-prs` (Cursor `split-to-prs`; quoted `AUTH:` before any outward push or PR publish; Must not replace `/sc-discuss` sizing or mid-run map resize; Must not merge; review hygiene; never required for ship; re-ready if the mission work branch mutates after `ready`).
- **Ship** → squash ≤5, closeout, merge `--no-ff`, archive. Roadmap continues: `Next: new session → /sc-discuss <id>`

capability tips (e.g. post-ready drain via `sc-post-ready-drain`; optional post-ready fat-diff hygiene via `sc-split-to-prs` / Cursor `split-to-prs` — quoted `AUTH:` before any outward push or PR publish; Must not replace `/sc-discuss` sizing or mid-run map resize, Must not merge, never required for ship; re-ready if the mission work branch mutates after `ready`; optional overnight/AFK `/sc-run` watch via `sc-loop` / `/loop` — stop or ready handoff → disarm + `handback.md`; optional Automations+Slack HIL AFK via `sc-automate-slack` — Slack notify on handback/needs-HIL, Slack reply may cue resume; Must not AUTH/`VERIFIED`/ship from Slack; Slack resume ≠ AUTH; never required for ready/ship; mission artifacts SoT; stop or ready handoff → disarm when armed; optional canvas-SoT via `sc-canvas-sot` for plan|findings|evidence human-check emits — disposition `Canvas-sot:`; Must not treat canvas as AUTH/`VERIFIED`/ready/ship; Canvas ≠ ready proof; never required for ready/ship; primary UI/workflow probe executor via `sc-browser-probe` Browser matrix — Cursor IDE browser (`cursor-ide-browser`) first; browser / MCP / chat success Must not authorize `ready` / `VERIFIED` / `AUTH` / ship) may run as Cursor-primary aids. Spacecraft still owns ready/ship (orchestration / pass-fail). Never soft-pass ready/ship from Cursor chat tables alone. Opened split PRs are never ready or ship proof.

Findings: fix in `/sc-run` and report in the summary (no issue ledgers). Roadmap CLI: `spacecraft map use|current|next`.

## Sizing / roadmap (hard Must)

≤7 jigsaw tasks per phase as a **hard Must** (not preference-only; reject soft prefer ≤7; reject any 8-9 exception band). Over that: same-mission `plan-phaseN.json` (`Sizing: phases`) or multi-mission via discuss mission-sizing (`*-data` → `*-functional` → `*-ui` → optional `*-integrate`). Planning must not `map new` - stop for `/sc-discuss` resize. Full protocol: `sc-discuss/references/mission-sizing.md`.

## Mission resolution

Branch `feat/<id>/…` → `.space/missions/<id>/`. Clarify: `open` | `clear` | `deferred`. CLI: `evidence`/`evi`, `validate`/`val`, `roadmap`/`map`, `set-state`.

## Lanes (pointers)

- **Discuss:** sizing, lens, spec, decisions, visual draft, mission brief. Skills: `sc-clarify`, `sc-ux-design`, `sc-storm` (Tier 3 research only). House look: root `DESIGN.md` + `150-design.mdc` on UI globs.
- **Mission:** plan → design-contract → approved-scenarios → build → fix → browser-probe (UI/workflow) → review → ready. Skills: `sc-planning`, `sc-tdd`, `sc-verification`, `sc-browser-probe`, `sc-judge` (ready only on `VERIFIED`). Port look from approved draft; sync tokens into `DESIGN.md`.
- **Polish:** one-off polish/optimize/refactor/adjust stays `/sc-quick`. Batched work is mission-class with evidence — trigger ≥3 items in `.space/polish-backlog.md` OR explicit batch discuss; max ≤5 files/batch; backlog `.space/polish-backlog.md`.
- **Ship / Quick / Debug:** matching slash skill. Quick skips mission ceremony but not INTENT / AUTH / TWINS / 3-cycle.

## Subagent Delegation

Orchestrator, not implementer. Task: `sc-coder`, `sc-tester`, `sc-planner`, `sc-reviewer` (+ `sc-judge` before ready), `sc-designer`, `sc-adviser`, `sc-firmware`, `sc-writer`, `sc-browser-probe` (UI/workflow live sweep + fix-loop).

Patterns: draft approved in discuss before run; run ports look (draft-parity); tester before coder; writer for docs/prose triage skips; UI/workflow → Task(`sc-browser-probe`) to `PROBE: CLEAN` before review; ready only on `VERIFIED`.

## Graph vs Loop

`/sc-run` and `/sc-ship` are a **graph** (disk state + machine-checkable edges). Keep **loops** for discuss research, Debug, `sc-storm`, and `/sc-quick` one-offs.

## Inner-loop (Quick + Mission)

Also `000-spacecraft`. TWINS: after defect fixes, project-wide search for the same construct before claiming done. After **3 failed fix-verify cycles**, stop and hand back to human.
